IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`

§ `Chapter 23 -- Attempts`

-- Penal Code 1871 s 511.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.

§§ `Section 511 -- Attempt to commit offence`

-- A person attempts to commit an offence who, with the intention of committing
-- that offence, takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence.
-- An act is a substantial step if it is strongly corroborative of an intention
-- to commit the offence. s 511(3): unknown impossibility does not prevent attempt.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 511"
@export Decide whether the facts constitute an attempt under Penal Code 1871 section 511
GIVEN t IS AN Attempt @desc Intention to commit an offence punishable by this Code or any other written law, plus a substantial step that is strongly corroborative of that intention. Examples in s 511(2) include lying in wait, enticing the victim, reconnoitring, unlawful entry, possession of specially designed materials, and soliciting an innocent agent. Unknown impossibility does not prevent attempt (s 511(3)).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an attempt` IF
        t's `intends to commit an offence punishable by this Code or any other written law`
    AND t's `takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence`
    AND t's `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence`

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an attempt` IF
        `constitutes an attempt` (a's `attempt`)
    AND NOT (`a general exception applies` a)

§§ `Illustrations`

`substantial step` MEANS Attempt WITH
    `intends to commit an offence punishable by this Code or any other written law` IS TRUE
    `takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence` IS TRUE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS TRUE
    `facts unknown to the actor make the doing of the thing impossible` IS TRUE

`bare intention` MEANS Attempt WITH
    `intends to commit an offence punishable by this Code or any other written law` IS TRUE
    `takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence` IS FALSE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS FALSE
    `facts unknown to the actor make the doing of the thing impossible` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `constitutes an attempt` `substantial step`
#ASSERT NOT (`constitutes an attempt` `bare intention`)

